Everyone asks: "What happens in a recession?"

Here's my exact playbook:

Phase 1: Recognition (VIX >30, unemployment rising)
→ Close all CSPs at 50% profit
→ Move 80% to cash
→ Keep 20% in quality stocks

Phase 2: Panic (market down 20%+)
→ Do nothing
→ Watch everyone else panic sell
→ Make a shopping list

Phase 3: Opportunity (RSI <30 on weekly)
→ Buy LEAPs on QQQ, AAPL, MSFT
→ 360 DTE, 10% OTM
→ Use 30% of cash

Phase 4: Recovery (market bounces)
→ Scale out at 100% gains
→ Return to normal CSP strategy
→ Bank the profits

Recessions don't scare me.
They're the biggest opportunity.

But only if you have a plan.

